Outside of building software and studying computer science, I spend time behind the camera as a photographer for NECC Esports and campus events.

### Fast glass and dark arenas

Esports photography brings an interesting set of constraints: dark stages, intense monitor backlights, rapidly changing stage LEDs, and players whose expressions shift in fractions of a second during high-stakes clutch rounds.

Balancing shutter speed to freeze micro-reactions without blowing out sensor noise requires knowing your gear intimately. It is a completely different mental space from writing code, but shares that same pursuit of precision and framing.
